#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# hermite_h

#% text
# `hermite_h(n, x)` gives the Hermite polynomial H_n(x).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# At a non-negative integer degree the polynomial is expanded in its argument (evaluated for numbers).

#% item
# At other numeric degrees the hypergeometric representation gives the value; symbolic degrees stay unevaluated.

#% item
# The physicists' normalization: H_1(x) = 2x.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
hermite_h(3, x)
#% output
#= -12*x + 8*x^3

#% cell
hermite_h(4, 0.5)
#% output
#= 1.0

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
hermite_h(2.5, 0.7)
#% output
#= -2.3223265248560367

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `laguerre_l`, `legendre_p`
